2) Apply principles and practices of integrated product support management to achieve H-1 in-service Software and Avionics Test (SWAT) program goals and objectives;
3) Responsible for the integration management, coordination, and execution of Software and Avionics Test (SWAT) logistics effort focusing on the Integrated Product Support concept and the Twelve Product Support Elements (PSEs);
4) Applying continuous improvement methods to identify opportunities for life cycle cost reductions and improvement of aircraft and subsystems availability;
5) Providing inputs to Program IPTLs/PSM/PDAPMLs to assist in the development of logistics support budgetary requirements to meet aviation program objectives. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
